From 8dfc8e311b0efba69f6a4dd2b41c0189be81ddef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bherbruck <brennen.herbruck@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:07:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(motion): the axis fit reads flats hiding in a fine
 ball's latitudes

A finely meshed UV ball puts every facet's normal line through its
centre, so a rod or flat bar through that centre shared its pencil, and
the ball's continuous latitudes swallowed the rod's faces into one wide
class the ring check skips: a trusted cross axis that would turn a
100 mm rod into a disc. Wide classes are now cut into latitude bins whose
bearings must not fold (1st-4th harmonic resultant); a pencil whose
folded area passes 2 % of the inliers does not bear the axis out.

Fixes #237

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
